# NIR_Mistral Framework - Ventoy Stick Setup

## 🚀 Overview

This Ventoy stick contains a complete **NIR_Mistral Framework** deployment with:
- **Django Server** running on port {{ django_port }}
- **Port Management Agent** running on port {{ port_agent_port }}
- **Cross-platform support** (Windows/Linux/Mac)
- **Docker integration** for containerized deployments

## 📋 What's Included

### Core Components
- **Django Project**: Full NIR_Mistral Django application with REST API
- **Port Agent**: Comprehensive port management system with conflict resolution
- **Virtual Environment**: Python {{ ansible_python_version }} with all dependencies
- **Systemd Services**: Automatic startup and management

### Features
✅ **Automatic Port Management**: No more port conflicts
✅ **REST API**: Full API access to port management features
✅ **Django Integration**: Seamless integration with Django applications
✅ **Docker Support**: Manage Docker container ports
✅ **Cross-platform**: Works on Linux, Windows, and Mac
✅ **Thread-safe**: Safe for concurrent access
✅ **Persistent Configuration**: Settings saved across reboots

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Method 1: Using the Startup Script (Recommended)

```bash
# Start all services
{{ deploy_root }}/start_nir_mistral.sh start

# Check status
{{ deploy_root }}/start_nir_mistral.sh status

# View logs
{{ deploy_root }}/start_nir_mistral.sh logs

# Stop all services
{{ deploy_root }}/start_nir_mistral.sh stop

# Restart services
{{ deploy_root }}/start_nir_mistral.sh restart
```

### Method 2: Using Systemd Services

```bash
# Start Django server
sudo systemctl start django

# Start Port Agent
sudo systemctl start port_agent

# Enable auto-start on boot
sudo systemctl enable django
sudo systemctl enable port_agent

# Check status
sudo systemctl status django
sudo systemctl status port_agent

# View logs
journalctl -u django -f
journalctl -u port_agent -f
```

## 🌐 API Endpoints

### Django Server (Port {{ django_port }})

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/api/health/` | GET | Health check |
| `/api/ports/` | GET | Port management overview |
| `/api/ports/status/` | GET | Detailed port status |
| `/api/ports/scan/` | GET | Scan ports in range |
| `/api/ports/check/<port>/` | GET | Check specific port |
| `/api/ports/reserve/` | POST | Reserve a port |
| `/api/ports/release/` | POST | Release a port |
| `/api/ports/conflicts/` | GET | Get port conflicts |

### Port Agent (Port {{ port_agent_port }})

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `/api/ports/` | GET | Port management status |
| `/api/ports/scan/` | GET | Scan port range |
| `/api/ports/check/<port>/` | GET | Check port availability |
| `/api/ports/assign/` | POST | Assign a free port |
| `/api/ports/reserve/` | POST | Reserve specific port |
| `/api/ports/release/` | POST | Release reserved port |
| `/api/ports/conflicts/` | GET | Detect port conflicts |
| `/api/ports/resolve/` | POST | Resolve port conflicts |

